  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "upfsGvyomyWPwBOjY7GKxoukva0=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:22.666Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "eligamo AG embeds Flowable in its own bank front-office product. As with the other OEM entries in the sweep, the research records the consequence rather than the relationship: vendor, not an integrator.\n\nThe pattern across the sweep is the more useful finding. At least three of the entries mined from the Flowable Partner Finder on 2026-08-18 are OEMs \u2014 Avaloq in core banking, Exentra in project controlling, eligamo in bank front-office \u2014 and two of the three build for banks. A vendor's partner directory rewards anyone shipping its engine, whether they resell delivery capacity or quietly compile it into a product, so the list conflates two populations that need opposite treatment.\n\nFor eligamo specifically, that leaves nothing actionable in the current record. The row was not imprint-swept, no principal or contact was resolved, and the only substantive claim is the OEM classification itself.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**unprioritised**\n- eligamo AG (CH) \u2014 eligamo.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> OEM PARTNER \u2014 embeds Flowable in its own bank front-office product. Vendor, not an integrator \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:22.666802Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:22.666806Z"
    }
  },
